{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yjh6cdrrhr2prbhfm3ygctixamunntrqct54dphhtwrghgcrxjfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both files are written, compile clean, and are behaviourally verified.\n\n## Files written\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-NMiSQO/translation/src/rng.rs` — 395 lines\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-NMiSQO/translation/src/randombytes.rs` — 93 lines\n\nNo other file was created or modified.\n\n## Errors\nZero errors and zero warnings originating in my two files. `cargo build --release` in the crate currently fails before type-checking with target-resolution / `E0583` errors for sibling modules still being written in parallel (`src/main.rs`, `fors`, `merkle`, `sign`, `utilsx1`, `wotsx1`, `backend/thash_haraka`, …), so `grep -E \"rng.rs|randombytes.rs\"` on the build output is empty. To get real verification I copied both files verbatim into a throwaway crate in `$TMPDIR` with only `aes = \"0.8\"` and the same `Cargo.lock`; both compile with no diagnostics.\n\n## Correctness verification\nRan the NIST PQC KAT seeding sequence from `app/src/PQCgenKAT_sign.c` (`entropy_input[i] = i`, `randombytes_init(entropy_input, NULL)`, then repeated `randombytes(seed, 48)`):\n```\nseed0 = 061550234D158C5EC95595FE04EF7A25767F2E24CC2BC479D09D86DC9ABCFDE7056A8C266F9EF97ED08541DBD2E1FFA1\nseed1 = D81C4D8D734FCBFBEADE3D3F8A039FAA2A2C9957E835AD55B22E75BF57BB556AC81ADDE6AEEB4A5A875C3BFCADFA958F\n```\nThese match the canonical `count = 0` / `count = 1` seed values present in every NIST PQC `.rsp` file, so the AES-256-CTR-DRBG is byte-identical to the OpenSSL-backed C version.\n\nAlso confirmed the exported C symbols in a `cdylib` build are the plain names with no collision: `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update`, `randombytes`, `randombytes_init`, `seedexpander`, `seedexpander_init`.\n\n## Notes on translation decisions\n- `EVP_aes_256_ecb` + single 16-byte `EVP_EncryptUpdate` maps exactly to one `aes::Aes256::encrypt_block`; no OpenSSL binding used.\n- `DRBG_ctx` is `static mut DRBG_CTX` reached through `addr_of_mut!`, as instructed.\n- To get the exact plain C symbol names *and* keep the safe Rust functions with the same identifiers, the five `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"` wrappers live in a nested `pub mod ffi` inside `rng.rs`. Rust item names there are identical to the C names (`rng::ffi::randombytes`, etc.), and `nm` confirms the emitted symbols are unmangled and plain. Callers wanting the safe API use `rng::randombytes` as before.\n- `seedexpander`'s `x == NULL -> RNG_BAD_OUTBUF` check is unreachable through the safe `&mut [u8]` signature, so it is preserved in the `ffi::seedexpander` wrapper.\n- `randombytes_init` mirrors the C signature exactly (no `security_strength` parameter), with the 48-byte `seed_material` copy and the `if (personalization_string)` NULL guard as `Option`.\n- `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update` copies `provided_data` into a local `[u8; 48]` in the FFI wrapper purely to satisfy the borrow checker; no caller aliases `provided_data` with `Key`/`V`.\n- All counter increments use `wrapping_add`, though the `!= 0xff` guard means they can never actually wrap.\n- One deliberate divergence in `randombytes.rs`, documented inline: C does `i = (unsigned long long)read(fd, x, i)`, so a `read()` failure yields `(u64)-1` which passes the `i < 1` test and then advances the pointer by ~2^64 (undefined behaviour). I map a read error onto the same `sleep(1); continue;` retry path C takes for a zero-length read. This is unreachable for `/dev/urandom` and is not a behaviour change on any non-UB execution. The retry-on-open-failure loop, the 1 MiB chunk cap, the `sleep(1)` on short read, and the `static int fd` cached across calls are all reproduced. Note this file's `randombytes` is intentionally *not* `#[no_mangle]` (CMake builds it into the separate non-deterministic `sphincs_core` `.so`); `randombytes_urandom` is provided as the raw-pointer form."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":284,"cache_read_input_tokens":45635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":284,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Dw8CoF8SdVSRmxdd3GrZwe","session_id":"eb87ec4e-54f9-48e5-a5c6-d85aefaf339c","uuid":"2aede3cb-54be-4d59-8f83-330a6c609b90","timestamp":"2026-09-02T11:59:17.846Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate rng.c and randombytes.c"}
