{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zwchoi5r5brrul53bfpwminjuizuducmc5fgvbmm24rmfw7ryjca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. All three files written, the whole crate builds clean, and I verified byte-identical output against the C reference.\n\n## Files written (only these)\n| File | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-NMiSQO/translation/src/backend/haraka.rs` | 985 |\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-NMiSQO/translation/src/backend/hash_haraka.rs` | 172 |\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-NMiSQO/translation/src/backend/thash_haraka.rs` | 142 |\n\n## Build status\n`cargo build --release` (default `haraka,robust,128s`) finishes with **zero errors and zero warnings**; `grep -E \"haraka\"` on the build output is empty. Also verified clean for all 12 combinations of `{128s,128f,192s,192f,256s,256f} x {robust,simple}`.\n\n## Differential validation against C (the important part)\nI built the C reference (`haraka.c`, `hash_haraka.c`, `thash_haraka_{robust,simple}.c`) into a scratch driver and a mirror Rust driver (copies of my files + real `address`/`utils` helpers), dumping: tweaked 512/256 round-constant tables (640/320 raw bytes), `haraka512`, `haraka512_perm`, `haraka256`, `haraka_S` over 15 input lengths (0..100) and 8 output lengths (1..70, exercising the non-multiple-of-32 tail), `prf_addr`, `thash` for every `inblocks` 1..SPX_FORS_TREES, `gen_message_random`, and `hash_message` (digest + `tree` + `leaf_idx`). **All 12 configurations matched exactly** (Rust built in debug mode, so no arithmetic-overflow panics either). Scratch dirs were removed afterwards; nothing outside my three files was touched.\n\n## Notable translation decisions\n- `haraka.c` contains **no** `load_constants`, `haraka512_perm_zero`, `haraka256_sk`, `aesenc`, `mix256` or `mix512` — this is the constant-time BearSSL-derived bitsliced variant. Translated its statics: `br_dec32le`, `br_range_dec32le`, `br_enc32le`, `br_range_enc32le`, both bitslice S-boxes, `br_aes_ct{,64}_ortho`, `add_round_key{,32}`, `shift_rows{,32}`, `rotr16`/`rotr32`, `mix_columns{,32}`, `br_aes_ct64_interleave_{in,out}`, `interleave_constant{,32}`, `haraka_S_absorb`, `haraka_S_squeezeblocks`, and the `haraka512_rc64` table. The two S-boxes (identical circuits, u64 vs u32) and the three `SWAPN` widths are generated by `macro_rules!` so both instantiations are textually the same code as the C macros.\n- C calls `haraka512_perm(s, s, ctx)` with **aliasing** pointers (in `haraka_S_absorb`, `haraka_S_squeezeblocks`, `haraka_S_inc_*`). Since the C body decodes all 64 input bytes into `w` before writing any output, I added a private `haraka512_perm_inplace()` that copies to a 64-byte temp and forwards — bit-exact, and keeps the required safe signature `haraka512_perm(&mut [u8], &[u8], &SpxCtx)`.\n- The C VLAs (`SPX_VLA`) became fixed stack arrays: `haraka_S_absorb`'s `t` is `[u8; HARAKAS_RATE]` (r is only ever 32), and `thash`'s `buf`/`bitmask` are sized by a compile-time `MAX_INBLOCKS = max(SPX_WOTS_LEN, SPX_FORS_TREES, 2)`. No heap allocation.\n- `hash_haraka.rs`: `SPX_TREE_MASK`/`SPX_LEAF_MASK` consts reproduce `(~0)>>(64-SPX_TREE_BITS)` / `(~0u32)>>(32-SPX_LEAF_BITS)`, with a `== 0` arm only so rustc's constant-shift-overflow lint doesn't reject the (dead, `SPX_D == 1`) branch — no current parameter set has `SPX_D == 1`. The `#if SPX_TREE_BITS > 64 #error` became `const _: () = assert!(SPX_TREE_BITS <= 64);`.\n- `s_inc[64] += (uint8_t)mlen` and `s_inc[64] -= (uint8_t)i` use `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_sub` to match `uint8_t` semantics.\n- C ABI wrappers added: `SPX_thash`; `SPX_initialize_hash_function`, `SPX_prf_addr`, `SPX_gen_message_random`, `SPX_hash_message`; plus (since every function in `haraka.h` has the namespace `#define`) `SPX_tweak_constants`, `SPX_haraka_S_inc_{init,absorb,finalize,squeeze}`, `SPX_haraka_S`, `SPX_haraka512_perm`, `SPX_haraka512`, `SPX_haraka256`. `haraka.c` declares no non-static functions absent from the header.\n\nNo remaining errors or warnings attributable to my files."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":270,"cache_read_input_tokens":102057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":270,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01NWPghsdofLHUtd1CS7btEp","session_id":"eb87ec4e-54f9-48e5-a5c6-d85aefaf339c","uuid":"d5bf27f9-fce3-4bb0-9721-ffb14c9212ce","timestamp":"2026-09-02T12:01:59.976Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate haraka backend"}
