{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5ined2yj2nc3n66vim6einmycu7cfifnw24nagorfwywzszby5kq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `translation/src/sign.rs` written (486 lines), compiles with **zero errors and zero warnings**; the whole crate now builds and `cargo run --release --bin driver` produces a KAT transcript digest (`83F5A066…D532` for the default haraka/robust/128s config).\n\n## What was translated\n\nAll 10 functions from `c_src/app/src/sign.c`, plus the 10 `#[unsafe(export_name = \"...\")]` `extern \"C\"` wrappers with `_c`-suffixed Rust identifiers so the linker symbols are the plain C names from `api.h`.\n\nKey fidelity points:\n\n- **No namespacing.** I checked every header `sign.c` includes: `SPX_NAMESPACE()` is applied only to symbols owned by `address.h`, `fors.h`, `hash.h`, `merkle.h`, `thash.h`, `utils.h`, `wots.h`. Nothing defined *in* `sign.c` is namespaced, so all exports keep plain names — no `SPX_` prefixes here.\n- **`randombytes` source.** `app/CMakeLists.txt` builds `sphincs_core_det` from the common objects + `src/rng.c` (not `src/randombytes.c`), so both call sites (`crypto_sign_keypair` and the `optrand` draw in `crypto_sign_signature`) route through `crate::rng::randombytes`.\n- **Pointer arithmetic** on `sig` is reproduced with an explicit running `off: usize`, and every callee gets an exactly-sized subslice (`SPX_FORS_BYTES`, `SPX_WOTS_BYTES + SPX_TREE_HEIGHT*SPX_N`, etc.) matching what the C code reads/writes through the raw pointer. I verified against the now-present sibling modules that they index internally, so exact-length slices are compatible.\n- **`crypto_sign` ordering.** The task brief said the C code memmoves the message *first, then* signs. That is not what the code does — `crypto_sign_signature(sm, ...)` runs first, and `memmove(sm + SPX_BYTES, m, mlen)` second. I kept the actual C order. (Irrelevant for the driver, which passes disjoint `m`/`sm`, but it would matter if they aliased.)\n- **`crypto_sign_open` failure path.** Again contra the brief: the reference code sets `*mlen = 0` (not `-1`) on both failure paths, after `memset(m, 0, smlen)`. Reproduced as written. The one deliberate deviation is a `min(smlen, m.len())` clamp on that `fill(0)` so a short output slice cannot panic — in C an `m` shorter than `smlen` is already out-of-bounds UB, and the driver always passes `mlen + CRYPTO_BYTES`, so this never changes emitted bytes.\n- `crypto_sign_seed_keypair` stages the `memcpy(pk, sk + 2*SPX_N, SPX_N)` and the final `pk + SPX_N` copy through a `[u8; SPX_N]` temporary, since `sk` is borrowed mutably in Rust where C had two independent pointers.\n- Index updates use `(tree & ((1u64 << SPX_TREE_HEIGHT) - 1)) as u32`, preserving the C truncation into `uint32_t idx_leaf`.\n\n## Note on cross-checking against C\n\nI tried building the C reference out-of-tree to diff KAT digests, but `app/src/rng.c` needs `openssl/conf.h` and no OpenSSL headers are installed in this sandbox, so `sphincs_core_det` won't compile. The prebuilt `dt_keep/cdrv_*` binaries and `.out` traces were present when I first listed the directory but had been removed by the time I tried to run them, so a byte-level equivalence check against C is still outstanding and will need to happen wherever the reference toolchain is available."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":310,"cache_read_input_tokens":66179,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":310,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BdSQCP5w2vaJpqCDXgFG9u","session_id":"eb87ec4e-54f9-48e5-a5c6-d85aefaf339c","uuid":"205343bc-8760-4614-ad5a-852ece87352b","timestamp":"2026-09-02T12:02:12.392Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate sign.c"}
