*zero errors and zero warnings** from my three files for every `sha2,{robust|simple},<secpar>` combination.\n\n## Notes on the translation\n\n- `crypto_hashblocks_sha256/512` use a `W[64]`/`W[80]` schedule; I verified the `EXPAND_32`/`EXPAND_64` macro chains are exactly the standard recurrence (the rotating-`w0..w15` form reads the already-updated words in precisely the `W[t-16..t-2]` positions), so the result is identical. Round-constant tables were extracted mechanically from the C source, not typed by hand. All adds use `wrapping_add`.\n- `sha256_inc_finalize`'s `in += inlen; inlen &= 63; in -= inlen;` pointer dance is reproduced as `let inlen = inlen_full & 63; let tail = &input[inlen_full - inlen..];`. `bytes` uses `wrapping_add`, and the `(bytes << 3) as u8` / `(bytes >> 53) as u8` truncations are kept verbatim.\n- `SPX_N >= 24` (the `shaX` selector in `hash_sha2.c`) is a `const bool`, so the `if USE_512 {...}` dispatch folds away; `SPX_SHA512` in `thash` is likewise a runtime-folded `if`. `thash_512` is always compiled (harmless: `state_seeded_512` always exists in the Rust `SpxCtx`) but dead when `SPX_SHA512 == 0`.\n- `SPX_INBLOCKS`'s `& -SPX_SHAX_BLOCK_BYTES` became `& !(SPX_SHAX_BLOCK_BYTES - 1)`. The `>> (64 - SPX_TREE_BITS)` / `>> (32 - SPX_LEAF_BITS)` masks are precomputed consts guarded against the `SPX_D == 1` (`SPX_TREE_BITS == 0`) case that C never evaluates, so const-eval can't trip an overflow error.\n- `shaX(buf, buf, ...)` (in-place aliasing in `gen_message_random`) is reproduced via a temp: the C code consumes all input before writing output, and only the first `SPX_SHAX_OUTPUT_BYTES` of `buf` are overwritten. Likewise `shaX_inc_finalize(buf + BLOCK, state, buf, ...)` uses `split_at_mut`.\n- C VLAs (`SPX_VLA`) became stack arrays sized by a `MAX_INBLOCKS` const (= `max(SPX_FORS_TREES, SPX_WOTS_LEN, 2)`, covering every call site) with a heap fallback so the safe API stays total for out-of-range `inblocks`. `mgf1_*` does the same with a 192-byte cap; no allocation happens on any real path.\n- Namespacing follows the headers: `sha256*`/`sha512*` are exported unprefixed, `SPX_mgf1_256`, `SPX_mgf1_512`, `SPX_seed_state`, `SPX_prf_addr`, `SPX_thash`, etc. are prefixed.\n\nOne incidental observation (not touched, not mine): `src/main.rs:160` has an `unused_imports` warning for `use sphincs_core_det as spx;`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1590,"cache_read_input_tokens":127888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1590,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WaXKS8XprE22nfXUJRt5xy","session_id":"eb87ec4e-54f9-48e5-a5c6-d85aefaf339c","uuid":"50897f17-2e1b-46ac-a2a2-f9183386b5fa","timestamp":"2026-09-02T12:05:31.202Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate sha2 backend"}
