g>.stdout`, `.stderr`, `.rc`). Re-invoking it reuses an existing binary, so re-verifying any config is cheap.\n- `cref_harness/out/all48.tsv` — the complete regenerated 48-row table, useful for future diffing against a Rust port.\n- Per-config artifacts in `cref_harness/out/` and build logs in `cref_harness/logs/`.\n\nTwo notes on things I did not touch: `c_src/` and `translation/` were left entirely alone, and all binaries linked dynamically (the `-static` path in `build.sh` falls back as documented, since this host has no `libc.a`) — this is the same link mode used for the original 9 results, so the outputs are directly comparable."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3782,"cache_read_input_tokens":30520,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3782,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01X3fTFGLAzWzhwnntX8eVnF","session_id":"eb87ec4e-54f9-48e5-a5c6-d85aefaf339c","uuid":"cf630b68-bf07-4079-a43a-667e284a3ffe","timestamp":"2026-09-02T12:21:13.446Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Generate remaining C reference outputs"}
