{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_znmmyffvv3egcjv5inhhe7ww5jbueufelwva4m4gwmd47xlxp4yq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. **All 48 build configurations produce byte-identical stdout to the C reference binary.**\n\n## What was built\n\n`translation/` — pure-Rust SPHINCS+ crate, no C, no OpenSSL bindings (`aes` crate for AES-256-ECB in the NIST DRBG).\n\n| Layer | Rust files |\n|---|---|\n| Shared config | `params.rs`, `context.rs`, `lib.rs` |\n| Core | `address.rs`, `utils.rs`, `utilsx1.rs`, `wots.rs`, `wotsx1.rs`, `fors.rs`, `merkle.rs`, `sign.rs` |\n| RNG | `rng.rs` (AES-256-CTR-DRBG), `randombytes.rs` (/dev/urandom variant) |\n| Backends | `backend/{haraka,hash_haraka,thash_haraka}.rs`, `{sha2,hash_sha2,thash_sha2}.rs`, `{fips202,hash_shake,thash_shake}.rs`, `{blake256,blake512,hash_blake,thash_blake}.rs` |\n| Driver | `main.rs` (all four KAT-transcript variants) |\n\nEvery `.c` file has a complete equivalent; ~8,400 lines of Rust.\n\n## Feature gates (CMake cache variables → lowercase Cargo features)\n\n- `HASH_BACKEND` → `haraka`, `sha2`, `shake` (+`shake256` alias), `blake`\n- `THASH` → `robust`, `simple`\n- `SECPAR` → `128s`, `128f`, `192s`, `192f`, `256s`, `256f`\n- `default = [\"haraka\", \"robust\", \"128s\"]`, matching the CMake defaults. Explicitly requested features take precedence over the defaults, so both `--no-default-features --features \"sha2,simple,192f\"` and `--features \"sha2,192f\"` select correctly.\n\n`[lib] crate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"rlib\"]` + `[[bin]] name = \"driver\"`. Linker symbols honour the `SPX_NAMESPACE(s) → SPX_##s` macro (`SPX_thash`, `SPX_prf_addr`, …) while non-namespaced ones (`crypto_sign*`, `sha256`, `shake256`, `blake256`, `randombytes`, `seedexpander`) keep plain names.\n\n## Verification\n\nBuilt the original C with a self-contained AES shim (no OpenSSL available) and generated reference digests for all 48 configs → `reference_outputs.txt`. Rust matched **48/48**. All 48 also compile warning-free.\n\nTwo original-C quirks were reproduced rather than fixed: `hash_blake.c`/`PQCgenKAT_sign.c` pass *byte* counts to BLAKE's *bit*-count `update` API, and `gen_message_random` for BLAKE overruns `R` with bytes that are later overwritten."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":974,"cache_read_input_tokens":190710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":974,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb87ec4e-54f9-48e5-a5c6-d85aefaf339c","uuid":"3bbede3c-c6de-48bc-977a-0bd49242082b","timestamp":"2026-09-02T12:35:55.381Z"}
